{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.104,
            0.295,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "COORDINATE GEOMETRY"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.104,
            0.898,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "107"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.138,
            0.902,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "Draw AR, PS and BT perpendicular to the x-axis. Draw AQ and PC parallel to the x-axis. Then, by the AA similarity criterion,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.183,
            0.534,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { \\scriptsize ~ P A Q } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { \\scriptsize ~ B P C }",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.223,
            0.206,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.256,
            0.156,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": "Now,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.209,
            0.702,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{ PA }{ BP } = \\frac{ AQ }{ PC } = \\frac{ PQ }{ BC } \\quad &(1) \\\\& AQ  =  RS  =  OS  -  OR  = x - x_{_1} \\\\& PC  =  ST  =  OT  -  OS  = x_{_2} - x \\\\& PQ  =  PS  -  QS  =  PS  -  AR  = y - y_{_1} \\\\& BC  =  BT  -  CT  =  BT  -  PS  = y_{_2} - y_{_1}\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.349,
            0.472,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "Substituting these values in (1), we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.432,
            0.17,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "Taking"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.48,
            0.253,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": "Similarly, taking"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.375,
            0.704,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{m_{1}}{m_{2}} &= \\frac{x - x_{1}}{x_{2} - x} = \\frac{y - y_{1}}{y_{2} - y} \\\\\\frac{m_{1}}{m_{2}} &= \\frac{x - x_{1}}{x_{2} - x}, \\quad \\text { we get } x = \\frac{m_{1}x_{2} + m_{2}x_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}} \\\\\\frac{m_{1}}{m_{2}} &= \\frac{y - y_{1}}{y_{2} - y}, \\quad \\text { we get } y = \\frac{m_{1}y_{2} + m_{2}y_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}}\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.522,
            0.899,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ the coordinates of the point $\\mathrm{P}(\\bar{x}, \\bar{y})$ which divides the line segment joining the points $\\mathrm { A } ( \\boldsymbol { x } _ { 1 } , \\boldsymbol { y } _ { 1 } )$ and $\\mathbf { B } ( x _ { _ 2 } , y _ { _ 2 } )$ , internally, in the ratio $m _ { _ 1 } : m _ { _ 2 }$ are"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.333,
            0.573,
            0.897,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{m_{1}x_{2} + m_{2}x_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}}, \\frac{m_{1}y_{2} + m_{2}y_{1}}{m_{1} + m_{2}} \\right)\\tag{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.622,
            0.526,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "This is known as the section formula"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.647,
            0.899,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": "This can also be derived by drawing perpendiculars from A, P and B on the y-axis and proceeding as above."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.691,
            0.9,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "If the ratio in which P divides AB is k : 1, then the coordinates of the point P will be"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.718,
            0.608,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{kx_{2} + x_{1}}{k + 1}, \\frac{ky_{2} + y_{1}}{k + 1} \\right).",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.772,
            0.899,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "Special Case : The mid-point of a line segment divides the line segment in the ratio 1 : 1. Therefore, the coordinates of the mid-point P of the join of the points $\\mathrm { A } ( x _ { 1 } , y _ { 1 } )$ and $\\mathbf { B } ( x _ { 2 } , y _ { 2 } )$ is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.829,
            0.741,
            0.874
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{1 \\cdot x_{1} + 1 \\cdot x_{2}}{1 + 1}, \\frac{1 \\cdot y_{1} + 1 \\cdot y_{2}}{1 + 1} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2}, \\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{2} \\right)",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.879,
            0.713,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "Let us solve a few examples based on the section formula."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
